THOUGHT: `resolution` is a @Nullable field, but `getResolution()` returns non-null. The simplest safe fix is to lazily initialize `resolution` from the current graphics configuration when it is null, similar to how `renderCanvas` is initialized, ensuring a non-null return without changing annotations or other behavior. I’ll update `getResolution()` accordingly.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '205,207c\  public Dimension getResolution() {
    if (this.resolution == null) {
      this.resolution = Game.config().graphics().getResolution();
    }

    return this.resolution;
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/GameWindow.java
```

